{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"frangible-applicable-snipe","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\n\nBug b636 (landed as 5e7d6e71ba) added deleted-source recovery to fsck: `restore_deleted_sources` (src/rebar/_commands/fsck_repair.py:662) writes deleted pre-images back as `.retired`, and `rebuild_with_restore` (:714) composes that restore with `rebuild_snapshot_from_full_log` before rebuilding.\n\nOnly ONE call site actually uses the composed helper — fsck_repair.py:596. The per-ticket repair path `_repair_ticket` (:208) still calls `rebuild_snapshot_from_full_log` DIRECTLY at :269-271, so it rebuilds from whatever sources survive and never attempts the restore. That path fails closed rather than corrupting anything, but a ticket whose SNAPSHOT source was dropped by legacy compaction is not recovered when repair runs through `_repair_ticket`.\n\nDiscovered while closing story 9f7f (superseded into b636): every other acceptance criterion of 9f7f is implemented, this call site is the residual gap.\n\n## Plan\n\nRoute `_repair_ticket`'s rebuild through `rebuild_with_restore` so the two repair entry points behave identically, and surface any restored sources in the same `disp` reporting shape the other path uses. Confirm no double-restore when both paths run in one fsck invocation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `_repair_ticket` obtains its rebuild through `rebuild_with_restore`, not a direct `rebuild_snapshot_from_full_log` call.\n- [ ] Restored source paths are reported from the `_repair_ticket` path the same way the :596 path reports them.\n- [ ] A held-out test proves a ticket whose SNAPSHOT source was deleted by legacy compaction is recovered when repair runs via `_repair_ticket` (RED before the change).\n- [ ] A test proves running both repair paths in one invocation does not double-restore or double-report.\n- [ ] Existing fsck repair and restore tests pass unchanged.","id":"08c8-b6b2-4da6-4373","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"fsck _repair_ticket bypasses rebuild_with_restore, so repair never restores deleted SNAPSHOT sources"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786313724101886001,"uuid":"fcaf6e06-9307-43d4-b990-3a436a2ca066"}